  "preamble": "Retroflexion of the alveolar affricate [ts] to the retroflex stop [ʈ] retracts the tongue tip and drops the fricative release. Puyuma, a Formosan language of southeastern Taiwan, shows this for Proto-Austronesian *C, which Blust reconstructs as a voiceless alveolar affricate: *Capa 'smoke fish or meat' became trapa and *Caŋis 'cry' became ʈangis, where the official orthography writes /ʈ/ as ⟨tr⟩. Neighbouring Paiwan keeps an affricate (tsangitj 'cry', capa 'smoke'), and Kavalan and Bunun have plain t (tapa, tangis).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Retroflexion, Deaffrication",
